<title>SPAIN: Spain's Argentaria 1996 net falls 57.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain's Argentaria 1996 net falls 57.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996 results for Spain's Corporacion Bancaria de Espana (Argentaria), in billions of pesetas, unless stated</p>
<p> Net attributable profit	    31.22     vs    74.20</p>
<p> Net profit			     35.11     vs    73.61</p>
<p> Pretax profit			  42.03     vs    84.94</p>
<p> Net interest income		 196.77     vs   207.20</p>
<p> Ordinary income		     273.77     vs   259.88</p>
<p> Operating income		     89.58     vs    82.32</p>
<p> Interest income		     926.33     vs 1,002.16</p>
<p> Interest expenses		   738.20     vs   800.73</p>
<p> Net fees and commissions	   47.25     vs    41.65</p>
<p> Financial/trading income	   29.75     vs    11.03</p>
<p> Operating costs		     162.36     vs   159.98</p>
<p>  -personnel costs		   116.45     vs   114.59</p>
<p>  -general, admin. costs	    45.91     vs    45.39</p>
<p> Depreciation			   17.86     vs    13.59</p>
<p> Other operating income	     -3.98     vs    -3.99</p>
<p> Net earnings from equity-accounted</p>
<p>    holdings			     4.98     vs     4.03</p>
<p> Amortisation of goodwill	    7.10     vs     2.24</p>
<p> Earnings on group transactions    2.09     vs     8.85</p>
<p> Loan-loss provisions		  9.74     vs    42.59</p>
<p>  -Net provision			31.78     vs    68.57</p>
<p>  -Principal recoveries	     22.04     vs    25.98</p>
<p> Extraordinary income/loss	 -36.87     vs    34.34</p>
<p> Corporate income tax		  6.92     vs    11.33</p>
<p> Minorities				3.90     vs    -0.59</p>
<p> Total dividend (pesetas)	    277	vs     270</p>
<p> BIS capital adequacy ratio	13.0 %     vs   13 pct</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
